ated and this is  done by vitamin k vitamin k works like a  coenzyme for gamma glutamine carboxylase  and this is how this process is  augmented by vitamin K now the  deficiency could be due to many reason  for example absorption defect in the  intestine or due to prolong consumption  of antibiotics which kill all the gut  microflora and guide gut microflora  plays a key role in absorption not only  in adults in infants vitamin K  deficiency could occur because in infant  the Guttman intestine is relatively  sterile and it doesn't have that much of  gut microflora as a result the vitamin  k1 absorption could be deficient so for  infant hemorrhage or infant blood clots  it is recommended intramuscular  injection of vitamin k and it is all  about this video I hope this video was  useful if you liked this video give it a  big thumbs up don't forget to Like share  and subscribe thank you
 

